.SS "void p6est_balance_ext (\fBp6est_t\fP * p6est, \fBp8est_connect_type_t\fP btype, int max_diff, int min_diff, \fBp6est_init_t\fP init_fn, \fBp6est_replace_t\fP replace_fn)"

.PP
2:1 balance the size differences of neighboring elements in a forest\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp6est\fP\fP The \fBp6est\fP to be worked on\&. 
.br
\fIbtype\fP Balance type (face or corner/full)\&. Corner balance is almost never required when discretizing a PDE; just causes smoother mesh grading\&. 
.br
\fImax_diff\fP The maximum difference between the horizontal refinement level and the vertical refinement level 
.br
\fImin_diff\fP The minimum difference between the horizontal refinement level and the vertical refinement level 
.br
\fIinit_fn\fP Callback function to initialize the user_data which is already allocated automatically\&. 
.br
\fIreplace_fn\fP Callback function that allows the user to change incoming quadrants based on the quadrants they replace\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void p6est_coarsen_columns_ext (\fBp6est_t\fP * p6est, int coarsen_recursive, int callback_orphans, \fBp6est_coarsen_column_t\fP coarsen_fn, \fBp6est_init_t\fP init_fn, \fBp6est_replace_t\fP replace_fn)"

.PP
Horizontally coarsen a forest\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp6est\fP\fP The forest is changed in place\&. 
.br
\fIcoarsen_recursive\fP Boolean to decide on recursive coarsening\&. 
.br
\fIcallback_orphans\fP Boolean to enable calling coarsen_fn even on non-families\&. In this case, the second quadrant pointer in the argument list of the callback is NULL, subsequent pointers are undefined, and the return value is ignored\&. If coarsen_recursive is true, it is possible that a quadrant is called once or more as an orphan and eventually becomes part of a family\&. 
.br
\fIcoarsen_fn\fP Callback function that returns true if a family of quadrants shall be coarsened\&. 
.br
\fIinit_fn\fP Callback function to initialize the user_data which is already allocated automatically\&. 
.br
\fIreplace_fn\fP Callback function that allows the user to change incoming quadrants based on the quadrants they replace\&. 
.RE
.PP

