.SS "\fBp6est_t\fP* p6est_copy_ext (\fBp6est_t\fP * input, int copy_data, int duplicate_mpicomm)"

.PP
Make a deep copy of a \fBp6est\fP\&. The connectivity is not duplicated\&. Copying of quadrant user data is optional\&. If old and new data sizes are 0, the user_data field is copied regardless\&. The inspect member of the copy is set to NULL\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIcopy_data\fP If true, data are copied\&. If false, data_size is set to 0\&. 
.br
\fIduplicate_mpicomm\fP If true, MPI communicator is copied\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Returns a valid \fBp6est\fP that does not depend on the input\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBp6est_t\fP* p6est_load_ext (const char * filename, sc_MPI_Comm mpicomm, size_t data_size, int load_data, int autopartition, int broadcasthead, void * user_pointer, \fBp6est_connectivity_t\fP ** connectivity)"

.PP
Load the complete connectivity/p6est structure from disk\&. It is possible to load the file with a different number of processors than has been used to write it\&. The partition will then be uniform\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIfilename\fP Name of the file to read\&. 
.br
\fImpicomm\fP A valid MPI communicator\&. 
.br
\fIdata_size\fP Size of data for each quadrant which can be zero\&. Then user_data_pool is set to NULL\&. If data_size is zero, load_data is ignored\&. 
.br
\fIload_data\fP If true, the element data is loaded\&. This is only permitted if the saved data size matches\&. If false, the stored data size is ignored\&. 
.br
\fIautopartition\fP Ignore saved partition and make it uniform\&. 
.br
\fIbroadcasthead\fP Have only rank 0 read headers and bcast them\&. 
.br
\fIuser_pointer\fP Assign to the user_pointer member of the \fBp6est\fP before init_fn is called the first time\&. 
.br
\fIconnectivity\fP Connectivity must be destroyed separately\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Returns a valid forest structure\&. A pointer to a valid connectivity structure is returned through the last argument\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Aborts on file errors or invalid file contents\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBp6est_t\fP* p6est_new_ext (sc_MPI_Comm mpicomm, \fBp6est_connectivity_t\fP * connectivity, \fBp4est_locidx_t\fP min_quadrants, int min_level, int min_zlevel, int num_zroot, int fill_uniform, size_t data_size, \fBp6est_init_t\fP init_fn, void * user_pointer)"

.PP
Create a new forest\&. This is a more general form of \fBp6est_new()\fP\&. See the documentation of \fBp6est_new()\fP for basic usage\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fImpicomm\fP Used und remembered in the result\&. 
.br
\fIconnectivity\fP Valid connectivity of tree topologies\&. 
.br
\fImin_quadrants\fP Minimum initial quadrants per processor\&. Makes the refinement pattern mpisize-specific\&. 
.br
\fImin_level\fP The forest is horizontally refined at least to this level\&. May be negative or 0, then it has no effect\&. 
.br
\fImin_zlevel\fP The forest is vertically refined at least to this level\&. May be negative or 0, then it has no effect\&. 
.br
\fInum_zroot\fP The number of 'root' vertical layers (used when non-power-of-2 layers are desired) 
.br
\fIfill_uniform\fP If true, fill the forest with a uniform mesh instead of the coarsest possible one\&. The latter is partition-specific so that is usually not a good idea\&. 
.br
\fIdata_size\fP Size of per-quadrant stored user data\&. 
.br
\fIinit_fn\fP If not NULL, called on every quadrant created\&. 
.br
\fIuser_pointer\fP Stored as is in the result for later reference\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A valid forest structure\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBp4est_gloidx_t\fP p6est_partition_ext (\fBp6est_t\fP * p6est, int partition_for_coarsening, \fBp6est_weight_t\fP weight_fn)"

.PP
Repartition the forest\&. The forest is partitioned between processors such that each processor has an approximately equal number of quadrants (or weight)\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp6est\fP\fP The forest that will be partitioned\&. 
.br
\fIpartition_for_coarsening\fP If true, the partition is modified to allow one level of coarsening\&. 
.br
\fIweight_fn\fP A weighting function or NULL for uniform partitioning\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The global number of shipped quadrants 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void p6est_refine_columns_ext (\fBp6est_t\fP * p6est, int refine_recursive, int maxlevel, \fBp6est_refine_column_t\fP refine_fn, \fBp6est_init_t\fP init_fn, \fBp6est_replace_t\fP replace_fn)"

.PP
Horizontally refine a forest with a bounded refinement level and a replace option\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp6est\fP\fP The forest is changed in place\&. 
.br
\fIrefine_recursive\fP Boolean to decide on recursive refinement\&. 
.br
\fImaxlevel\fP Maximum allowed refinement level (inclusive)\&. If this is negative the level is restricted only by the compile-time constant QMAXLEVEL in \fBp4est\&.h\fP\&. 
.br
\fIrefine_fn\fP Callback function that must return true if a quadrant shall be refined\&. If refine_recursive is true, refine_fn is called for every existing and newly created quadrant\&. Otherwise, it is called for every existing quadrant\&. It is possible that a refinement request made by the callback is ignored\&. To catch this case, you can examine whether init_fn or replace_fn gets called\&. 
.br
\fIinit_fn\fP Callback function to initialize the user_data for newly created quadrants, which is guaranteed to be allocated\&. This function pointer may be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIreplace_fn\fP Callback function that allows the user to change incoming quadrants based on the quadrants they replace; may be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void p6est_refine_layers_ext (\fBp6est_t\fP * p6est, int refine_recursive, int maxlevel, \fBp6est_refine_layer_t\fP refine_fn, \fBp6est_init_t\fP init_fn, \fBp6est_replace_t\fP replace_fn)"

.PP
Vertically refine a forest with a bounded refinement level and a replace option\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp6est\fP\fP The forest is changed in place\&. 
.br
\fIrefine_recursive\fP Boolean to decide on recursive refinement\&. 
.br
\fImaxlevel\fP Maximum allowed refinement level (inclusive)\&. If this is negative the level is restricted only by the compile-time constant QMAXLEVEL in \fBp4est\&.h\fP\&. 
.br
\fIrefine_fn\fP Callback function that must return true if a quadrant shall be refined\&. If refine_recursive is true, refine_fn is called for every existing and newly created quadrant\&. Otherwise, it is called for every existing quadrant\&. It is possible that a refinement request made by the callback is ignored\&. To catch this case, you can examine whether init_fn or replace_fn gets called\&. 
.br
\fIinit_fn\fP Callback function to initialize the user_data for newly created quadrants, which is guaranteed to be allocated\&. This function pointer may be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIreplace_fn\fP Callback function that allows the user to change incoming quadrants based on the quadrants they replace; may be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void p6est_save_ext (const char * filename, \fBp6est_t\fP * p6est, int save_data, int save_partition)"

.PP
Save the complete connectivity/p6est data to disk\&. This is a collective operation that all MPI processes need to call\&. All processes write into the same file, so the filename given needs to be identical over all parallel invocations\&. See \fBp6est_load_ext()\fP for information on the autopartition parameter\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIfilename\fP Name of the file to write\&. 
.br
\fI\fBp6est\fP\fP Valid forest structure\&. 
.br
\fIsave_data\fP If true, the element data is saved\&. Otherwise, a data size of 0 is saved\&. 
.br
\fIsave_partition\fP If false, save file as if 1 core was used\&. If true, save core count and partition\&. Advantage: Partition can be recovered on loading with same mpisize and autopartition false\&. Disadvantage: Makes the file depend on mpisize\&. Either way the file can be loaded with autopartition true\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Aborts on file errors\&. 
.RE
.PP

